1
00:00:07,466 --> 00:00:09,301
- See, look!
- What is it?

2
00:00:09,343 --> 00:00:10,344
Isn't it crazy?

3
00:00:10,427 --> 00:00:12,387
It has to be CG, right?

4
00:00:12,596 --> 00:00:14,056
It's using electricity...

5
00:00:14,139 --> 00:00:17,184
Whoa, it blew
that Demon's head off!

6
00:00:17,518 --> 00:00:18,894
So cute!

7
00:00:19,686 --> 00:00:21,438
It's him!

8
00:00:21,522 --> 00:00:24,024
No, it's true!
I'm looking right at them!

9
00:00:24,650 --> 00:00:26,235
Something feels off.

10
00:00:26,443 --> 00:00:29,363
Everyone's looking
because I'm so cute!

11
00:00:29,780 --> 00:00:31,365
- There they are!
- Okay!

12
00:00:31,698 --> 00:00:33,992
Hey, come back here!

13
00:00:34,618 --> 00:00:36,119
This is bad.
Run!

14
00:00:37,871 --> 00:00:39,873
Yup, that's right, Mom.

15
00:00:39,957 --> 00:00:45,295
ROOSTER WARRIOR
TAKES DOWN A DEMON!!!

16
00:00:40,499 --> 00:00:42,793
It's already gotten over
a million views.

17
00:00:42,918 --> 00:00:44,962
I told you I could do it, right?

18
00:00:46,004 --> 00:00:50,676
Yup, I'll call you again.
I love you, Mom!

19
00:00:54,346 --> 00:00:57,307
I'm finally on my way to becoming
a famous viewtuber!

20
00:00:58,350 --> 00:01:03,855
<i>My original plan was to upload
videos of me hunting rare bugs...</i>

21
00:01:04,106 --> 00:01:07,150
<i>A whopping 9.5 centimeters!
It's huge!!</i>

22
00:01:08,527 --> 00:01:10,320
<i>That was until last week,</i>

23
00:01:10,362 --> 00:01:12,573
<i>when I was in the mountains
looking for bugs,</i>

24
00:01:14,157 --> 00:01:16,743
<i>I came across those chickens!</i>

25
00:01:17,786 --> 00:01:20,747
<i>After that, I tracked them
all the way to this city, but...</i>

26
00:01:21,164 --> 00:01:23,500
<i>It looks like I've lost them.</i>

27
00:01:24,960 --> 00:01:27,337
<i>But they should
still be around here.</i>

28
00:01:30,299 --> 00:01:32,217
<i>Those chickens are mine.</i>

29
00:01:32,884 --> 00:01:36,930
<i>I'm gonna hunt them down
and get the ultimate video!</i>

30
00:01:36,972 --> 00:01:39,057
- Wait!
- Hey!

31
00:03:22,994 --> 00:03:24,955
- Get back here!
- Get back here!

32
00:03:25,497 --> 00:03:26,748
There they are!

33
00:03:27,958 --> 00:03:28,959
There's some here too...

34
00:03:29,376 --> 00:03:30,752
All right!
We've got them trapped!

35
00:03:30,836 --> 00:03:32,045
We've got you!

36
00:03:32,295 --> 00:03:33,964
- Elizabeth, let's go up.
- Got it.

37
00:03:36,091 --> 00:03:38,802
- D-Damn it!
- They got away!

38
00:03:39,845 --> 00:03:42,764
EPISODE 5
THE MOTLEY FLOCK SCATTERS

39
00:03:44,349 --> 00:03:47,185
ROOSTER WARRIOR
TAKES DOWN A DEMON!!!

40
00:03:44,683 --> 00:03:47,184
Views on the video
keep growing.

41
00:03:47,185 --> 00:03:50,188
What do they intend on doing
if they catch us?

42
00:03:50,355 --> 00:03:52,190
Are they planning
on selling us to a circus?

43
00:03:52,357 --> 00:03:55,694
I know!
It's hard to be famous!

44
00:03:57,404 --> 00:04:00,197
I don't think we have a choice
but to hide here

45
00:04:00,198 --> 00:04:01,741
until things calm down.

46
00:04:02,033 --> 00:04:03,618
You want me to hide?

47
00:04:03,952 --> 00:04:05,704
You've gotta be joking.
I'm outta here.

48
00:04:06,663 --> 00:04:09,666
There's a lot of people in town
targeting us.

49
00:04:09,916 --> 00:04:11,084
It's suicide!

50
00:04:11,168 --> 00:04:14,796
Why do I have to hide from humans?!

51
00:04:15,130 --> 00:04:17,924
I live my life the way I choose!

52
00:04:18,091 --> 00:04:19,926
I'm just saying
you're gonna get caught!

53
00:04:20,010 --> 00:04:22,219
You're making a big mistake
if you underestimate humans!

54
00:04:22,220 --> 00:04:24,973
- I don't take orders from anybody!
- What?

55
00:04:25,182 --> 00:04:26,850
If I say I'm going, I'm going!

56
00:04:27,017 --> 00:04:30,270
Why are you so stubborn!
You birdbrain!

57
00:04:30,312 --> 00:04:33,023
Quit squabbling,
you hysterical woman!

58
00:04:33,273 --> 00:04:34,399
What is wrong with you?!

59
00:04:34,524 --> 00:04:37,109
You're the one who's throwing
a childish fit!

60
00:04:37,110 --> 00:04:40,363
- Huh?!
- Please don't fight!

61
00:04:43,074 --> 00:04:44,867
I'm done!

62
00:04:44,868 --> 00:04:46,578
Farewell, you two.

63
00:04:46,661 --> 00:04:47,496
- What?!
- What?!

64
00:04:47,579 --> 00:04:49,289
I'm continuing my travels alone.

65
00:04:50,123 --> 00:04:51,999
- Wait!
- Mister!

66
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:53,794
Don't go!

67
00:04:54,711 --> 00:04:57,339
- Piyoko!
- Mister!

68
00:04:57,422 --> 00:05:00,717
- Wait for me!
- You shouldn't leave either!

69
00:05:03,762 --> 00:05:06,807
<i>Damn it.
That woman pisses me off.</i>

70
00:05:08,099 --> 00:05:09,476
Got him!

71
00:05:17,234 --> 00:05:19,152
NEW PACHINKO MACHINES

72
00:05:22,030 --> 00:05:25,575
<i>Those are the machines
humans like to play with.</i>

73
00:05:26,034 --> 00:05:28,203
<i>I guess it wouldn't hurt
to take a load off.</i>

74
00:05:34,084 --> 00:05:37,045
<i>How can they enjoy themselves
with all this racket?</i>

75
00:05:37,629 --> 00:05:39,381
<i>Humans are crazy...</i>

76
00:05:45,887 --> 00:05:46,888
<i>I see...</i>

77
00:05:46,972 --> 00:05:48,932
<i>If you line up the pictures,
you receive money...</i>

78
00:05:50,559 --> 00:05:52,310
<i>Wanna give it a try?</i>

79
00:05:55,146 --> 00:05:56,982
<i>Speaking directly to my mind?</i>

80
00:05:57,190 --> 00:06:00,235
<i>Also, this scent...
there's no mistake.</i>

81
00:06:01,111 --> 00:06:02,112
You're...

82
00:06:02,195 --> 00:06:03,697
A Demon aren't you?

83
00:06:06,825 --> 00:06:07,826
<i>That's right.</i>

84
00:06:08,451 --> 00:06:10,912
<i>Name's Morio.
I'm a Demon.</i>

85
00:06:11,371 --> 00:06:14,040
What's a Demon doing in
a place like this?

86
00:06:14,082 --> 00:06:15,792
<i>Cut it out with the mean face.</i>

87
00:06:16,042 --> 00:06:18,837
<i>I don't care much for fighting.</i>

88
00:06:19,880 --> 00:06:21,923
<i>True, I don't sense any violence
or bloodlust.</i>

89
00:06:22,757 --> 00:06:25,010
<i>I'll let you try it out
if you want.</i>

90
00:06:36,855 --> 00:06:37,772
Oh!

91
00:06:37,939 --> 00:06:39,566
I could get used to this!

92
00:06:39,691 --> 00:06:41,192
<i>You're pretty good.</i>

93
00:06:41,526 --> 00:06:42,527
Sir.

94
00:06:43,737 --> 00:06:45,697
Pets are forbidden inside.

95
00:06:49,409 --> 00:06:51,286
- Oh my!
- What is it?

96
00:06:51,494 --> 00:06:54,289
I was just playing with a coin
I picked up off of the ground...

97
00:06:54,456 --> 00:06:57,334
and now look at the amount
I'm walking out with!

98
00:06:58,543 --> 00:07:01,296
<i>So he didn't have that money
to begin with...</i>

99
00:07:01,796 --> 00:07:03,089
<i>If it's money that he found...</i>

100
00:07:03,173 --> 00:07:05,925
<i>It wouldn't hurt him if he spread
the wealth around a bit...</i>

101
00:07:07,010 --> 00:07:09,220
<i>I wanna eat sea urchin!!</i>

102
00:07:09,471 --> 00:07:12,474
But this kinda doesn't feel right.

103
00:07:12,766 --> 00:07:13,767
I'm gonna go return it.

104
00:07:15,310 --> 00:07:17,937
- What is it?
- Uh, I mean,

105
00:07:18,021 --> 00:07:19,981
it was your luck
that earned you the winnings!

106
00:07:20,106 --> 00:07:25,278
To waste such a gift from god...
would be a sin.

107
00:07:25,320 --> 00:07:27,405
So, it's okay if I accept this?

108
00:07:27,489 --> 00:07:29,491
O-Of course!

109
00:07:30,075 --> 00:07:31,076
By the way...

110
00:07:32,535 --> 00:07:34,746
I want to talk to you about something.

111
00:07:35,830 --> 00:07:37,749
RAW SEA URCHIN 90% OFF!!

112
00:07:39,793 --> 00:07:42,462
I didn't know chickens ate
stuff like this.

113
00:07:43,046 --> 00:07:45,799
<i>Oh, my darling sea urchin...</i>

114
00:07:46,424 --> 00:07:49,135
<i>How I've dreamed of you!</i>

115
00:08:01,773 --> 00:08:04,401
<i>What is this unbelievably
disgusting-tasting sea urchin?!</i>

116
00:08:04,901 --> 00:08:06,403
<i>Is it rotten?</i>

117
00:08:06,611 --> 00:08:09,739
<i>It's totally different from
fresh sea urchin!</i>

118
00:08:10,156 --> 00:08:14,703
- <i>I thought I could finally eat it...</i>
- H-Hey...

119
00:08:14,744 --> 00:08:18,039
<i>...and satisfy my craving!</i>

120
00:08:20,375 --> 00:08:23,044
<i>My sea urchin!!</i>

121
00:08:26,256 --> 00:08:27,298
Rooster!

122
00:08:27,716 --> 00:08:29,718
Hey, Rooster!

123
00:08:29,926 --> 00:08:32,637
Rooster!

124
00:08:38,393 --> 00:08:39,769
You awake?

125
00:08:39,894 --> 00:08:40,812
Where am I?

126
00:08:41,271 --> 00:08:42,480
This is my home.

127
00:08:42,856 --> 00:08:47,360
You passed out on me,
so I carried you back here.

128
00:08:48,028 --> 00:08:50,071
I see.
I owe you one.

129
00:08:51,114 --> 00:08:52,866
Do you live alone here?

130
00:08:53,033 --> 00:08:55,952
That's right.
I've lived here for a while now.

131
00:08:56,161 --> 00:08:58,705
Sometimes I go into town for fun...

132
00:08:59,497 --> 00:09:00,331
But...

133
00:09:01,207 --> 00:09:03,501
This is where I'm most comfortable.

134
00:09:04,335 --> 00:09:07,213
It's quiet and the view is great.

135
00:09:08,256 --> 00:09:09,632
It's my favorite spot.

136
00:09:13,094 --> 00:09:14,554
Where's the human who created you?

137
00:09:15,221 --> 00:09:18,767
He's probably happily
living his life somewhere.

138
00:09:21,019 --> 00:09:24,189
I was born about 6 months ago.

139
00:09:26,816 --> 00:09:29,486
I'm sorry, but you have
terminal stomach cancer,.

140
00:09:30,445 --> 00:09:33,239
You have about
a month left to live.

141
00:09:37,285 --> 00:09:42,207
<i>For 47 years,
I led a completely uneventful life.</i>

142
00:09:43,458 --> 00:09:45,585
<i>I've never even had a girlfriend.</i>

143
00:09:49,839 --> 00:09:53,176
Why was I born to begin with?

144
00:09:55,845 --> 00:09:59,099
I don't want to die...
I want to live more!

145
00:10:00,100 --> 00:10:02,393
I want to live...
I want to live!

146
00:10:03,103 --> 00:10:05,480
I want to live!

147
00:10:15,198 --> 00:10:19,786
I was born out of
your strong desire to live!

148
00:10:20,120 --> 00:10:22,914
So you can go
and die with no regrets!

149
00:10:23,873 --> 00:10:27,544
I'll live on for the both of us!

150
00:10:29,587 --> 00:10:32,090
<i>But that doesn't mean
anything... to me!</i>

151
00:10:35,343 --> 00:10:37,512
Huh?
It's the hospital.

152
00:10:38,471 --> 00:10:40,431
- Yes?
- <i>Oh, Mr. Morio!</i>

153
00:10:40,515 --> 00:10:42,976
<i>It appears
you don't have cancer at all!</i>

154
00:10:43,059 --> 00:10:43,893
What?

155
00:10:44,018 --> 00:10:45,019
<i>I'm so sorry!</i>

156
00:10:45,145 --> 00:10:47,647
<i>I must have gotten your chart
mixed up with someone else's!</i>

157
00:10:47,730 --> 00:10:49,607
<i>There's nothing
wrong with you.</i>

158
00:10:49,732 --> 00:10:51,025
<i>You're completely healthy!</i>

159
00:10:51,151 --> 00:10:53,319
YAIKI CLINIC
CALL ENDED

160
00:10:54,529 --> 00:10:55,947
I can go on living.

161
00:10:56,281 --> 00:10:57,991
Uh...
What about meâ€”?

162
00:10:58,032 --> 00:11:00,826
All right!
I can live!

163
00:11:00,827 --> 00:11:04,205
I'm going to try my best to live as if I
were reborn!

164
00:11:04,247 --> 00:11:07,041
- I'm gonna go find a girlfriend!
- Hey, wait... Hold on!

165
00:11:09,294 --> 00:11:12,964
I was supposed to live life
in his place.

166
00:11:13,590 --> 00:11:15,800
I was born a fluke.

167
00:11:16,009 --> 00:11:18,595
I'm a creature with no purpose.

168
00:11:19,220 --> 00:11:24,434
People in town bully me
and call me a monster.

169
00:11:24,601 --> 00:11:27,020
<i>- You monster!
- Get outta here!</i>

170
00:11:27,770 --> 00:11:29,189
<i>- Get him! Get him!
- Hey!</i>

171
00:11:31,691 --> 00:11:33,860
I'm sad.

172
00:11:34,694 --> 00:11:37,280
And my body keeps shrinking.

173
00:11:39,490 --> 00:11:43,453
In this world, there's no such
thing as a meaningless life.

174
00:11:45,330 --> 00:11:46,915
So just keep on living.

175
00:11:47,332 --> 00:11:49,834
You'll stumble upon
your purpose soon enough.

176
00:11:50,585 --> 00:11:53,713
Some people aren't alive
even if we want them to be.

177
00:11:55,006 --> 00:11:56,549
<i>Isn't that right, Sarah?</i>

178
00:11:58,468 --> 00:12:00,220
You're a good guy!

179
00:12:01,596 --> 00:12:02,764
Hardly.

180
00:12:02,847 --> 00:12:04,807
Oh! Wait right here!

181
00:12:06,059 --> 00:12:08,019
Taa-daa! It's sake!

182
00:12:06,392 --> 00:12:10,772
DAIGINJO SAKE "MUD"
SANJI SAKE BREWERY

183
00:12:08,019 --> 00:12:10,772
I got it with the money I earned
with my part time job at the factory.

184
00:12:10,813 --> 00:12:13,024
I'm in a drinking mood today.

185
00:12:13,274 --> 00:12:14,609
Will you join me?

186
00:12:14,859 --> 00:12:16,778
Heh, guess I've got no choice.

187
00:12:17,362 --> 00:12:18,696
I'll join you.

188
00:12:22,075 --> 00:12:25,245
I never knew having a drink
with someone tastes this good!

189
00:12:25,411 --> 00:12:27,538
This is so fun!

190
00:12:27,830 --> 00:12:31,042
So this is what
being drunk is like.

191
00:12:31,251 --> 00:12:32,794
Not bad.

192
00:12:33,378 --> 00:12:38,132
Ahh!
Something's rising up inside of me!

193
00:12:39,926 --> 00:12:41,844
What's wrong?

194
00:12:42,679 --> 00:12:43,972
I'm fine.

195
00:12:44,597 --> 00:12:48,893
I'm gonna show you
something special today.

196
00:12:49,185 --> 00:12:50,561
Watch this!

197
00:12:50,937 --> 00:12:53,606
It's the Chicken Dance.

198
00:12:55,608 --> 00:12:57,527
What a strange dance!

199
00:13:05,868 --> 00:13:07,203
You threw up again!

200
00:13:09,831 --> 00:13:12,875
This was the most fun
I've had in my entire life.

201
00:13:13,418 --> 00:13:15,211
Thank you, Keiji!

202
00:13:16,546 --> 00:13:18,756
Now I know there are Demons
like you out there.

203
00:13:19,507 --> 00:13:21,467
I'm glad I met you, Morio.

204
00:13:22,885 --> 00:13:24,178
- Later.
- Yup.

205
00:13:24,595 --> 00:13:25,888
Until our paths cross again!

206
00:13:29,100 --> 00:13:32,312
See you later, Keiji!

207
00:13:32,562 --> 00:13:34,439
See you later!

208
00:13:39,610 --> 00:13:43,072
<i>Now... to find a place
to sleep tonight.</i>

209
00:13:44,282 --> 00:13:45,992
<i>I wonder where they are now...</i>

210
00:13:47,827 --> 00:13:48,995
<i>Not my problem.</i>

211
00:13:56,461 --> 00:13:59,297
<i>A dangerous storm is brewing...</i>

212
00:14:06,596 --> 00:14:09,182
Mister!

213
00:14:09,474 --> 00:14:12,101
Where are you?!

214
00:14:12,351 --> 00:14:14,144
- What are you doing, Piyoko?!
- Mister!

215
00:14:14,145 --> 00:14:16,481
- We have to go somewhere safe!
- Mister!

216
00:14:16,731 --> 00:14:17,814
- It's so dark,
- Mister!!

217
00:14:17,815 --> 00:14:19,192
- you can't see a thing!
- Mister!!

218
00:14:19,984 --> 00:14:21,360
Get a hold of yourself!

219
00:14:21,611 --> 00:14:23,863
Keiji left and
he's left this town already!

220
00:14:24,072 --> 00:14:27,075
Just forget about
that horrible man!

221
00:14:27,200 --> 00:14:30,368
I'm going to follow him forever!

222
00:14:30,369 --> 00:14:32,121
I don't want to leave his side!

223
00:14:32,205 --> 00:14:36,667
Why did you stick around
if you hate him so much?!

224
00:14:36,709 --> 00:14:39,128
You always bully him...

225
00:14:39,337 --> 00:14:40,630
I feel so bad for him!

226
00:14:40,797 --> 00:14:44,884
You're terrible!
I hate you!

227
00:14:49,305 --> 00:14:50,807
Oh, a chicken!

228
00:14:52,100 --> 00:14:54,811
And a chick too!
Are they mother and child?

229
00:14:55,478 --> 00:14:57,688
Wow!
You're so fashionable!

230
00:14:57,772 --> 00:15:00,065
You have some words written
on your back...

231
00:15:00,066 --> 00:15:01,692
How cute!

232
00:15:01,859 --> 00:15:04,237
Oh, no, you're drenched!

233
00:15:04,862 --> 00:15:05,947
You're gonna catch a cold.

234
00:15:06,072 --> 00:15:09,158
Wait...
Can chickens catch colds?

235
00:15:09,200 --> 00:15:10,492
YES, WE CAN.

236
00:15:10,493 --> 00:15:13,621
Anyways,
what are you doing out here?

237
00:15:13,871 --> 00:15:14,956
Are you lost?

238
00:15:17,458 --> 00:15:19,418
Do you want to come home with me?

239
00:15:21,546 --> 00:15:23,339
I'm home, Grandpa!

240
00:15:24,132 --> 00:15:25,215
<i>We followed her here,</i>

241
00:15:25,216 --> 00:15:26,926
<i>since she seemed like
a good kid, but...</i>

242
00:15:28,719 --> 00:15:30,221
Yay!

243
00:15:30,263 --> 00:15:32,765
So many little pools!

244
00:15:32,890 --> 00:15:35,393
Here, Grandpa,
I brought your medicine.

245
00:15:36,227 --> 00:15:39,355
- Thank you, Misuzu.
- Splash-splash!

246
00:15:39,438 --> 00:15:41,941
<i>Thank you for helping us, Misuzu.</i>

247
00:15:42,483 --> 00:15:43,484
What?!

248
00:15:44,152 --> 00:15:45,361
No way, did you just...

249
00:15:45,903 --> 00:15:49,073
<i>My name is Elizabeth,
I can use smartphones to talk.</i>

250
00:15:49,699 --> 00:15:52,160
<i>And this is Piyoko.</i>

251
00:15:52,702 --> 00:15:55,246
Don't introduce me without
asking permission!

252
00:15:55,454 --> 00:15:58,124
Wow! You are so smart!

253
00:15:58,291 --> 00:16:00,251
Grandpa, did you hear that?!

254
00:16:00,376 --> 00:16:02,086
Oh my!

255
00:16:04,630 --> 00:16:06,883
All I could find was some wheat.
Would you like some?

256
00:16:07,091 --> 00:16:08,968
<i>Thank you, we will have some.</i>

257
00:16:09,135 --> 00:16:10,928
Take your time and eat!

258
00:16:16,642 --> 00:16:19,103
<i>Do you two live here alone?</i>

259
00:16:19,145 --> 00:16:20,521
- It's delicious!
- Yes.

260
00:16:21,022 --> 00:16:23,983
My parents died in a car accident...

261
00:16:24,483 --> 00:16:26,819
so my grandfather took me in.

262
00:16:27,778 --> 00:16:28,779
<i>I see...</i>

263
00:16:29,447 --> 00:16:31,240
Okay!
The dishes are done!

264
00:16:31,616 --> 00:16:32,700
Next up...

265
00:16:35,494 --> 00:16:37,205
<i>Do you like studying?</i>

266
00:16:37,288 --> 00:16:38,164
Yup!

267
00:16:38,497 --> 00:16:40,333
I want to become a doctor.

268
00:16:40,875 --> 00:16:43,920
Then I can cure Grandpa
for free, right?

269
00:16:44,378 --> 00:16:46,547
I see...
This is an honorable child.

270
00:16:46,839 --> 00:16:48,507
She definitely has what it takes.

271
00:16:48,591 --> 00:16:50,259
<i>Who are you to say?</i>

272
00:16:51,219 --> 00:16:54,472
<i>I wanted to ask you something.</i>

273
00:16:54,597 --> 00:16:56,390
<i>I did some research online earlier,</i>

274
00:16:56,432 --> 00:16:57,892
<i>and it seems this area</i>

275
00:16:57,934 --> 00:17:00,144
<i>is experiencing
record levels of rainfall.</i>

276
00:17:00,394 --> 00:17:02,855
<i>The river is also very close by.</i>

277
00:17:03,814 --> 00:17:06,817
<i>Shouldn't you two evacuate?</i>

278
00:17:08,694 --> 00:17:10,112
No need to fret.

279
00:17:10,988 --> 00:17:17,662
I've lived here my entire life. In those
85 years, we've never had a disaster.

280
00:17:18,412 --> 00:17:20,915
The rain will soon stop.

281
00:17:21,999 --> 00:17:24,001
<i>I hope you're right...</i>

282
00:17:25,419 --> 00:17:26,963
<i>Evacuation alert.</i>

283
00:17:27,296 --> 00:17:29,840
<i>A flood warning has now been
issued for areas near the river.</i>

284
00:17:30,424 --> 00:17:34,512
<i>Please evacuate immediately.
We repeat...</i>

285
00:17:42,311 --> 00:17:45,898
<i>Why did you stick around
if you hate him so much?!</i>

286
00:17:46,607 --> 00:17:48,776
<i>The reason is...</i>

287
00:17:48,859 --> 00:17:52,905
<i>It's because I need his strength
to defeat the Demons.</i>

288
00:17:53,573 --> 00:17:55,658
<i>I just gave into
my animal instincts...</i>

289
00:17:56,450 --> 00:17:57,535
<i>Farewell...</i>

290
00:17:57,618 --> 00:17:59,745
<i>My anger born from that day</i>

291
00:18:00,621 --> 00:18:02,290
<i>will never fade.</i>

292
00:18:02,915 --> 00:18:05,501
<i>But when I finally found Keiji,</i>

293
00:18:05,751 --> 00:18:07,461
<i>I couldn't bring myself
to kill him.</i>

294
00:18:07,712 --> 00:18:11,090
<i>Why couldn't I resist him then?</i>

295
00:18:11,966 --> 00:18:15,469
<i>Do I still have feelings for him?</i>

296
00:18:15,761 --> 00:18:19,765
<i>I can't understand my own
feelings!</i>

297
00:18:23,144 --> 00:18:24,729
Hey! Is anyone in here?!

298
00:18:25,146 --> 00:18:26,814
Yes! I'll be right there!

299
00:18:27,940 --> 00:18:29,817
Didn't you hear
the evacuation alert?

300
00:18:30,151 --> 00:18:31,569
The river's flooded!

301
00:18:32,278 --> 00:18:33,279
What?!

302
00:18:34,155 --> 00:18:35,698
You're in a flood zone!

303
00:18:35,740 --> 00:18:37,241
The water will be here soon!

304
00:18:37,283 --> 00:18:38,492
Evacuate immediately!

305
00:18:38,618 --> 00:18:40,161
I'm going to check
on the other houses!

306
00:18:54,967 --> 00:18:56,135
That's the evacuation center!

307
00:18:56,969 --> 00:18:58,387
We're almost there, Grandpa!

308
00:19:03,643 --> 00:19:04,602
No way...

309
00:19:09,774 --> 00:19:11,150
It won't budge!

310
00:19:11,233 --> 00:19:13,069
The rear wheel is jammed!

311
00:19:17,239 --> 00:19:18,240
It's no use...

312
00:19:21,535 --> 00:19:22,578
Miss Elizabeth?

313
00:19:22,662 --> 00:19:24,580
<i>Don't give up until the very end!</i>

314
00:19:27,166 --> 00:19:29,210
<i>I remember now...</i>

315
00:19:30,211 --> 00:19:33,089
<i>Even though she had
no reason to like me...</i>

316
00:19:33,255 --> 00:19:35,383
<i>she saved me back then.</i>

317
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:41,097
<i>Even now, she's risking her life
to save these humans.</i>

318
00:19:42,306 --> 00:19:43,181
<i>That's right...</i>

319
00:19:43,182 --> 00:19:45,726
<i>On the day we first met,
she said...</i>

320
00:19:46,268 --> 00:19:50,606
<i>All these people around the world
shouldn't have to suffer.</i>

321
00:19:51,649 --> 00:19:52,650
<i>That's right...</i>

322
00:19:53,150 --> 00:19:54,485
<i>She's the kind of person</i>

323
00:19:54,568 --> 00:19:56,779
<i>who has to help people
who are in need.</i>

324
00:19:57,571 --> 00:19:59,240
<i>I see it now.</i>

325
00:19:59,699 --> 00:20:03,035
<i>Elizabeth...
is the embodiment of duty!</i>

326
00:20:01,701 --> 00:20:03,452
DUTY

327
00:20:07,707 --> 00:20:08,666
Piyoko!

328
00:20:10,710 --> 00:20:12,753
Please move!

329
00:20:13,170 --> 00:20:14,588
It's no use!

330
00:20:14,755 --> 00:20:16,590
Leave me here and go!

331
00:20:16,632 --> 00:20:18,801
Never!

332
00:20:22,096 --> 00:20:24,640
I'm not giving up.

333
00:20:24,890 --> 00:20:26,892
Misuzu!

334
00:20:27,017 --> 00:20:29,937
My true strength!!

335
00:20:30,271 --> 00:20:35,192
Full power!

336
00:20:47,371 --> 00:20:51,542
Thanks for saving us,
Miss Elizabeth and Piyoko.

337
00:20:51,834 --> 00:20:55,463
Thank you so much!

338
00:20:55,504 --> 00:20:58,174
<i>Hey, you old baldy!
Never give up!</i>

339
00:20:58,257 --> 00:21:01,427
<i>Don't die before
Misuzu grows up, got it?!</i>

340
00:21:03,345 --> 00:21:05,639
<i>If it weren't for
Piyoko's strength,</i>

341
00:21:05,848 --> 00:21:07,516
<i>we probably wouldn't have made it.</i>

342
00:21:07,975 --> 00:21:09,935
I love you, Misuzu!

343
00:21:10,603 --> 00:21:12,688
<i>Good job, Piyoko.</i>

344
00:21:13,898 --> 00:21:16,901
<i>Anyways...
That was crazy powerful!</i>

345
00:21:19,195 --> 00:21:20,529
This rain is crazy.

346
00:21:22,072 --> 00:21:23,699
I hope Keiji is okay.

347
00:21:27,620 --> 00:21:30,206
That vibration! What was that?

348
00:21:30,664 --> 00:21:31,707
From where?

349
00:21:32,291 --> 00:21:35,294
It's a warning
that danger's near.

350
00:21:41,258 --> 00:21:44,386
Oh no...
This is bad!

351
00:21:49,558 --> 00:21:51,352
It's the dam!

352
00:21:51,477 --> 00:21:54,563
That giant dam is gonna break!

353
00:21:55,689 --> 00:21:57,650
What do I do?

354
00:21:57,691 --> 00:22:01,070
If the dam breaks, and floods
the town...

355
00:22:01,445 --> 00:22:03,906
This town surrounded
on all sides by mountains...

356
00:22:03,948 --> 00:22:06,534
...will be completely submerged!!

357
00:23:49,887 --> 00:23:51,347
I'm Morio!

358
00:23:51,889 --> 00:23:53,891
I'm friends with Keiji.

359
00:23:54,058 --> 00:23:55,434
Also...

360
00:23:55,517 --> 00:23:57,770
Everyone, get out of here!

361
00:23:58,520 --> 00:24:00,898
Next time:
Built Like a Brick Coop

362
00:24:01,231 --> 00:24:04,401
Keiji, I'll never forget you.

363
00:24:04,902 --> 00:24:09,823
FAN ART CONTEST AWARDS

